cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Donghyunpe (동현페): a browser laboratory that runs the 1999 Game Boy Color version of Prince of Persia as a program translated to JavaScript with a redrawn heroine, with the starting level, remaining time, health, brick colour and music set through the esoteric language Donghyun-lang"
type: software
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24430550"
version: "0.33"
date-released: "2026-11-22"
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Dong Hyun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9883-0229"
    affiliation: "Inha University College of Medicine"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Raspberry-Kim/donghyun-lab20"
url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lab20/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyunpe is a browser-based, noncommercial toy in which Amolang, the
  sultan's daughter, runs, jumps and climbs through fourteen levels. It
  does not run a ROM file in an emulator: the 7,582 machine instructions
  that the 1999 Game Boy Color version of Prince of Persia actually
  executes were translated instruction by instruction into JavaScript,
  and the screen, sound, input, timing and save layers were newly
  written. A program written in the esoteric programming language
  Donghyun-lang prints five integers that are read in order as the
  starting level (1 to 14), remaining time in minutes (1 to 60), health
  units (1 to 9), brick colour (dark pastel yellow or the original) and
  music (off or on). The hero was replaced by 578 newly drawn frames of
  Amolang that follow the positions and poses of the original frames,
  with the original rule for hiding the character behind pillars. The
  title screen, password entry and ending scenes are not included; the
  shadow and the mirror image keep the original hero graphics. Input is
  keyboard or gamepad, with on-screen buttons on phones; a desktop with a
  keyboard is recommended. Version 0.33 shortens the "Engine and
  credits" section of the page (the testing note and two sentences of the
  rights note were removed); the game, the engine and the save format are
  unchanged from version 0.32.
  Rights: the translated program in pe/core.js and the 228,169 bytes of
  level, background, sound and table data in pe/data.js come from the
  original game and belong to its rights holders. They are in the
  repository and on the page without permission, are NOT under the MIT
  license, and are left out of the release bundles and of this archive
  (.gitattributes export-ignore), so this archive alone does not run the
  game or the engine tests. The MIT license
  applies only to the parts written for Donghyunpe (the page, the
  protocol and examples, the Amolang graphics, the display and sound
  layers and the game layer); the page fonts are under the SIL Open Font
  License. The original ROM file, the notes on it and the tools that
  translate it are not in this repository, so pe/core.js and pe/data.js
  cannot be rebuilt from the repository either. Prince of Persia is a
  trademark of Ubisoft; this work is unaffiliated with Ubisoft, Jordan
  Mechner, Red Orb Entertainment, Ed Magnin and Associates or Nintendo.
  Tests are automated runs; the game was not played to the end by a
  person and no real device was checked.
keywords:
  - platform game
  - Prince of Persia
  - Game Boy Color
  - static recompilation
  - esoteric programming language
  - JavaScript
